Subject: [PATCH] Report a disconnect when a roam fails

On Linux >= 6.0 a failed join while already associated leaves the
interface unable to connect again until it is torn down, in practice
until a reboot.

wl_bss_connect_done() reports the failure with cfg80211_connect_result()
but never calls cfg80211_disconnected(). Up to 5.19 that was harmless,
because __cfg80211_connect_result() cleared wdev->current_bss on any
result. Since the 6.0 MLO rework the state is wdev->connected, which only
__cfg80211_disconnected() clears. cfg80211_connect() then returns
-EALREADY for every new connect, and cfg80211_disconnect() does not call
into the driver because ssid_len is already 0.

When the failed join was a roam away from a live link, report that link
as disconnected, the same way the WLC_E_LINK down path does.
---
--- a/src/wl/sys/wl_cfg80211_hybrid.c
+++ b/src/wl/sys/wl_cfg80211_hybrid.c
@@ -2555,6 +2555,18 @@
 		    conn_info->req_ie_len, conn_info->resp_ie, conn_info->resp_ie_len,
 		    completed ? WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS : WLAN_STATUS_AUTH_TIMEOUT,	GFP_KERNEL);
 		WL_DBG(("Connection %s\n", completed ? "Succeeded" : "FAILed"));
+
+		if (!completed && test_and_clear_bit(WL_STATUS_CONNECTED, &wl->status)) {
+			// cfg80211 keeps a failed roam's old link marked connected and rejects every later connect with -EALREADY.
+			WL_ERR(("roam failed, reporting the old link as disconnected\n"));
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(4,2,0)
+			cfg80211_disconnected(ndev, 0, NULL, 0, GFP_KERNEL);
+#else
+			cfg80211_disconnected(ndev, 0, NULL, 0, false, GFP_KERNEL);
+#endif
+			wl_link_down(wl);
+			wl_init_prof(wl->profile);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return err;
